 "approvalMessage": {
  "approvalNumber": 24,
  "billId": {
   "basePrintNo": "A2344",
   "basePrintNoStr": "A2344-2021",
   "printNo": "A2344A",
   "session": 2021,
   "version": "A"
  },
  "chapter": 623,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 24 Chapter 623\n \n      MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 2344-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to food allergy\n        awareness in food service establishments and online food  order-\n        ing services\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  I  fully  support  the intent of this legislation, which would require\nrestaurants and food service establishments to post food allergy notices\nin view of all employees, and to include information for customers about\nnotifying the establishment of any food allergies they may have  on  all\nmenus.\n \n  However,  this bill needs three amendments to be effective. First, the\nDepartment of Agriculture and Markets must provide oversight of  grocery\nstores.  Second, food vendors need an option to proactively include food\nallergy information on menus, rather than allowing the customer to noti-\nfy the vendor of any allergies. Third, to ensure this critical  informa-\ntion  reaches all employees in the food service industry, the Department\nof Health and the Department of Agriculture and Markets must  also  make\nthe food allergy notice for employees available in additional languages.\n \n  On the basis of this agreement, I am signing this legislation.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2022
 },
